  "final_text": "The bug was in `minor_units()` in `invoicing/currency.py`. It lowercased the currency code and then checked it against `ZERO_DECIMAL`, whose entries are uppercase (`{\"JPY\", \"KRW\"}`). The check never matched, so JPY and KRW were treated as 2-decimal currencies. I changed `.lower()` to `.upper()`.\n\n`test_invoice_jpy` now passes, and so does the rest of the suite (8 tests). I didn't change any test files."
